\section{Introduction}
Borgu Fulfulde (ISO 639-3: fue; Glottocode: borg1235) is a Fula variety spoken mainly in the Borgou region of Benin. It uses a Latin script and has dialects including Bakuure, Korakuure, Juguure and Caabankeere. It is not known to be taught in schools. The search results show mostly religious materials, and no dictionary, grammar or educational material was found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school materials were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia article on Borgu Fulfulde: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borgu_Fulfulde}
\end{itemize}
No dictionary or grammar was found in the search results.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Scripture Earth page, listing the New Testament (Bible.is, YouVersion portion and an app): \url{https://www.scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=fue}
\item SIM report on completion of the Bible (New Testament 2011, Old Testament 2024): \url{https://www.sim.org/stories/borgu-fulfulde-bible-translation-completed-benin-fulani/}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network, Borgu Fulfulde: \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/fue}
\item Global Recordings Network, Bakuure dialect: \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/9922}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The completed Bible and the audio materials give some written and spoken text in the language. Secular educational materials, a dictionary and a grammar are not evident, so a curriculum would need to build them.
\end{document}
